I. Universal Contracts & Multi-Repo Intelligence
- Repository Contract: Enforce uniform PUD directory structures (.clanker/, content/, README.md) to standardize layout across repositories.
    - the contract must be specified. 
    - i think it could mandate no cource files in repo root
    - uniformity in .clanker dir across pud and clanker itself. clanker will have to carry shared assets of all types in a separate directory
- Multi-Repo / Metarepo Support: Support resolvers capable of peeking into external local repositories to manage GitHub Profile Repositories and multi-project workspaces.

II. Context value strategies:
- Use all available metadata when rendering a prompt
  - The configs contain much metadata which is not used
        - project, domain, and prompt names (`domain.name`, `prompt.name`)
- Try to find architectural answers to questions of LLM context production
    - see 'purported wisdom/Fractal Context Pattern.md' for an idea

III. Config Asset Hygiene, management
- Asset Lifecycle & Audit System
  - Track dangling assets, unused templates, and unreferenced workspace files.
  - Asset Sanity Inspection: Quick diagnostic tools ("wtf are the assets of this prompt") for payload visibility.
- Lookahead & Validation
  - Pre-flight validate fileset references, asset directories, and template paths during config ingestion to disallow silent failures.
- Asset Namespace Separation
  - Split internal operational assets from project-specific (PUD) assets to eliminate collisions.
- Dynamic Synchronization & Reuse
  - Support hot-reloading/re-validation of configuration on disk without app restarts.
  - Support named, bottom-level shared declarations (filesets, MD resolvers, prompt frags) to keep PUD configurations DRY.

IV. Automation & practicality concerns
- Enhanced Ship Role & Automation
  - Elevate the ship script into an active orchestration pipeline.
  - Use built-in compilation resolvers for automated artifact generation (packaging context archives, README compiling).
- Multi-Context LLM Workflows
  - Streamline reception and incorporation of LLM artifacts (refactor plans, doc updates, backlogs) with human oversight.
  - Stepwise Code Updates: Staging mechanism to receive code updates iteratively across multiple context resets without breaking app usability.
  - Follow-Up & Omission Resolver: Request dynamic follow-up context with explicit visibility into omitted/unshared workspace files.

V. User / otherpeople oriented
- 'Clanker clanker;' Identity: Frame LLM contexts as short-lived object instances (`clanker`) of a broader pattern (`Clanker`). 
   Reclaims the term to highlight understanding, lifecycle awareness, and practical empowerment over fear.
- Built-In Guidance ('F1' Prompts): Native, instant help routes for Clanker usage and operational prompts.
