VIII. App model V2: Dual workflow - dev cycles & repo mapping
I. Dev cycles - All from yaml configs.
Essentially what the system is today:
- Plan -> implement -> add to history doc -> repeat
- ..but reworks the entity model, making filesets the central artifact, while domains and prompts become reusable

1. Fileset: the central bottom-level entity. 
- only declared bottom level
- can be aggregated (set operation style)
    - so this + that = new fileset
- they reference domains by name to subscribe to them

2. Domains: bottom level too.
Domains are used to create reusable prompting contexts
- attach documents via the md resolver.
    - code standards
    - domain purpose docs

3. Prompts attach to domains. 
Attach prompt specific documents via md resolver
- mode instructions
- additional docs, doctrines, whatever becomes of that concept
The collection of prompts becomes the core workflow
- plan
- implement
- migrate to history
Prompts have an alt-mode, which only uses the prompt attached assets. This allows one to squeeze value out of an llm context
    - first full plan mode
        - then alt-implement
        - then alt-migrate
        - then so on
    - or start with implement
        - then alt-migrate
        - then alt-plan
        ..
Hit prompt key to get the prompt
.. then hit it again for the alt mode

Result: the model deepens a level
- today its select domain, select prompt, there you go
- new system? select fileset, select domain, select prompt (1x, 2x)-> there you go
    - can a single simple UI view support this?
        - we need 1 row for filesets, 2 rows for domains, and 1 for prompts

II. Config production / maintenance (selecting the files to make up a fileset)
Primary purpose: produce filesets to cover the repository in full
    - secondary, domain & prompt asset selection / production
Problems:
- There may be many types of repos
    - well organized repos
    - spaghettiburgers
